  "worked_solution": "The Cartesian product $Z\\times Z$ consists of all ordered pairs whose first coordinate belongs to $Z$ and whose second coordinate belongs to $Z.$\n\nIn this case, the schematic for ${Z}^{2}=Z\\times Z$ is shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072443/assets/fa14e54c0518f8f5e64d3ccb4f725bd0b3804fb197d7b90320398ebbf09d68d4.png)\n\nHence, the set $Y=Z\\times Z$ is given by\n\n$$\nY={(t,t),(t,u)(u,t),(u,u)}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"",
